WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:05.700
Hey youtubers it's Charlie, I hope you've
all had a chance to re-watch the finale a

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:12.700
couple times. Since we're heading into the
hiatus I wanted to start off my with my favorite

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:17.949
Season 4 moments. Since a lot of you have
asked for full on spoilery bonus videos I'm

00:00:17.949 --> 00:00:22.190
going to make an announcement about that after
my list, so be sure to stick around.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:26.570
Since this video is all season 4 stuff, hopefully
you've seen the episodes, but if you haven't

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:33.120
consider this a spoiler warning. Here we go,
Number 10 - The Reforging of Ice

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.850
I was so happy they decided to use this to
open the season. It's so haunting and hypnotic.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:41.810
They even played Rains of Castamere softly
in the background while it was all happening.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:46.280
I know a lot of you guys flipped when they
buried Widow's Wail with Joffrey but at least

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.850
we still have Oathkeeper roaming around the
Vale with Brienne.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:54.680
I remember when people started to talk more
and more about resurrection after Beric and

00:00:54.680 --> 00:01:00.010
Thoros were introduced, well both resurrection
and re-animation by the White Walkers.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:04.489
Like secretly everyone was trying to do the
mental math on Ned Stark being able to return

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:10.240
somehow. Either as a wight or with some crazy
Red God magic.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.549
But when you see Ice get melted down it's
like all your hopes get melted with it. The

00:01:15.549 --> 00:01:19.649
only way anyone would be able to restore Ice
now would be to dig up Joffrey's corpse and

00:01:19.649 --> 00:01:20.909
hunt down Brienne.

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:25.529
Not that reforging Ice would restore House
Stark or Winterfell, but it's one of those

00:01:25.529 --> 00:01:32.149
secret wishes I had the first time I read
about this scene and then again when I saw

00:01:32.149 --> 00:01:32.579
it.

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:36.240
My sympathies to book readers. Let me know
if you have that thing where you read about

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:42.859
this a long long time ago and forgot about
it until you saw it on screen. Like you were

00:01:42.859 --> 00:01:47.159
learning about it for the first time again
as if it were completely new.

00:01:47.159 --> 00:01:53.549
I know a lot of you guys have been reading
the books since the show started, but Book

00:01:53.549 --> 00:02:00.549
3 was published in 2000, that's like 14 years,
so a lot of times we have to re-read stuff.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.260
Number 9 - Shiny New Dragons

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:16.280
The dragons in general this year were amazing
as expected. That was one of the biggest effects

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.220
they were talking about during season 3, so
of course they had to top themselves for season

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:26.530
4. If you wondered why we didn't see a lot
of them in episodes. It's just because the

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:28.230
effects are super expensive to do.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:32.420
I'm looking forward to the day when a fully
digital creature can be nominated for a best

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:38.630
performance. The best dragon actor is of course
Benedict Cumberbatch as Smaug, Peter Jackson

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:43.230
full on mo capped his performance so that
dragon was much closer to being a real life

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:43.850
actor.

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.850
I don't think the dragons on Game of Thrones
are motion captured, mostly because they don't

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:51.400
speak words, but Drogon's acting was great.
He felt a lot more like a really big wild

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.170
dog or a domesticated tiger.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:58.670
Like something you could pet, but dangerous
enough that he could shred you by accident

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.640
if he wanted to play.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.550
The two biggest fandom questions I see everywhere
are whether or not Bran could ever warg a

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:11.140
dragon and how the psychic link between Targaryen's
and their Dragons works.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:14.800
George RR Martin has never given a definitive
answer about warging. He's only said there's

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:20.600
no precedent, no one in history has ever tried
it, or been recorded trying it. And he hasn't

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.300
gotten far enough into the books to explain
the minutiae of Targaryen Dragon Bonding.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:29.600
Far and away the best book about Targaryen's
relationships with their dragons is the short

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.880
story the Princess and the Queen. It's part
of that Dangerous Women Anthology. It covers

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:37.750
the Dance of the Dragons, one of the many
Targaryen Civil Wars that happened in history.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.230
So if you want to read more about Dragons
on Game of Thrones, that would be a good place

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:48.230
to start.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:53.800
Number 8 - The Purple Wedding and Joffrey's
Death

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.670
As amazing as this was, it was no Red Wedding.
And Joffrey's death wasn't even the biggest

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:02.810
thing I saw you guys talking about. It was
actually the dwarf jousting. That was the

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:07.270
biggest question I got, that and Penny just
because she had some emotional scenes with

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:07.630
Tyrion.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:12.780
I re-watched it a couple of times and I didn't
see any references to Penny but the dwarf

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:18.709
jousting completely lived up to expectations.
I think if you felt excited, and then immediately

00:04:18.709 --> 00:04:21.159
shameful for being excited about watching
dwarves degrade themselves, you were right

00:04:21.159 --> 00:04:23.210
where George RR Martin wanted you to be.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:28.039
There were a lot of moments where I found
myself cheering at really awful stuff on screen.

00:04:28.039 --> 00:04:31.849
Mostly because it's so fun to see stuff from
the books. And then immediately you process

00:04:31.849 --> 00:04:36.060
the moment and think, oh this really bad,
I'm a terrible person for cheering right now.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:39.669
And then Joffrey dies and suddenly you don't
have to feel ashamed about cheering.

00:04:39.669 --> 00:04:42.680
It's not something I've mentioned a lot but
one of the things I love most about the show

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:49.680
is the way it makes your really excited for
terrible terrible things. Like dwarf jousting.

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:57.659
Number 7 - Jaime and Cersei in Baelor's Sept
Over your own dead son's body, how could you?

00:04:57.659 --> 00:05:01.629
This was an infamous book moment that became
much more controversial on the show. At the

00:05:01.629 --> 00:05:06.370
end of the day I think what they intended
to do and what the audience saw were two different

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:12.710
things. I was a little disturbed, but I knew
it was going to happen, so I don't think I

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:15.419
was as outraged as people who only watch the
show.

00:05:15.419 --> 00:05:19.300
The thing that always stands out to me, aside
from the actual act of the sex, is the way

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:24.029
Jaime reacts to people calling him out as
the father of Cersei's children. They only

00:05:24.029 --> 00:05:27.710
time I've seen him acknowledge it in an obvious
way is when Tyrion called him out right after

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.840
he was thrown in prison after Joffrey died.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:36.840
When Cersei talked about 'their baby boy'
being dead in the Sept it almost looked like

00:05:38.439 --> 00:05:42.939
he was mentally blocking the thought. As he
was later in the finale when Cersei said she

00:05:42.939 --> 00:05:44.740
told Tywin what they had been doing.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:48.229
I think Jaime just doesn't want to think about
Joffrey or Cersei's children as being his,

00:05:48.229 --> 00:05:54.800
he doesn't want to deny it or acknowledge
it. He just wants to change the subject.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:01.800
I'll be interested to see if the show decides
to give more fatherly scenes to him with Tommen's

00:06:06.469 --> 00:06:07.319
character.

00:06:07.319 --> 00:06:09.900
Number 6 - Daario Takes Down The Champion
of Meereen

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:14.430
Pissing in the dust notwithstanding this was
a pretty meta scene. The really obvious homage

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:18.759
I saw was the Raiders of the Ark takedown.
But the biggest easter egg was something that

00:06:18.759 --> 00:06:23.279
I didn't learn about till much later. The
Champion is shouting insults from Monty Python

00:06:23.279 --> 00:06:25.569
translated into Low Valyrian.

00:06:25.569 --> 00:06:29.580
It was this really elaborate joke that D.B.
Weiss thought of. He's a huge Monty Python

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:34.069
fan, so he had the champion shout the Frenchman's
Insults from Holy Grail. But because they're

00:06:34.069 --> 00:06:39.129
really strict about diagetic speech, the person
who created the Valyrian Language translated

00:06:39.129 --> 00:06:44.210
the insults into low valyrian so it would
be authentic to george rr martin's world.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:48.379
Missandei translates the words as something
different, so there's no way you'd understand

00:06:48.379 --> 00:06:51.339
the Monty Python reference unless you could
speak Low Valyrian yourself.

00:06:51.339 --> 00:06:55.740
And if you can do that you deserve a giant
high five. Because you are awesome.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:58.360
Number 5 - Ser Pounce Makes a Rare Appearance

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:02.069
As much as the show changes things from the
books, I always get excited when they include

00:07:02.069 --> 00:07:06.430
things like Ser Pounce. He's a big part of
Tommen's character and as much as I disagree

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:10.999
with them aging him up so much, adding Ser
Pounce back in was icing on the cake. This

00:07:10.999 --> 00:07:15.939
was also in the same episode we got to see
the Lands of Always winter. So just in general

00:07:15.939 --> 00:07:18.069
there were a lot of hat tips to book readers.

00:07:18.069 --> 00:07:20.999
From what Michelle McLaren, the director of
that episode, said. We're not going to see

00:07:20.999 --> 00:07:25.270
Ser Pounce again. But that doesn't mean he
won't be referenced.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:30.150
Ser Pounce is a good indication that we might
get some Patchface references next season

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:36.770
too. I've got my fingers crossed. Dan and
Dave have a pretty decent track record for

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:41.150
squeezing in easter eggs when they're really
important for informing characters backstories.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:43.689
Number 4 - The Lands of Always Winter

00:07:43.689 --> 00:07:47.809
This was another one of those minor controversies
just because some book readers felt like it

00:07:47.809 --> 00:07:51.860
was spoilers for Winds of Winter and there
was the whole thing about the HBO website

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.680
spoiling the Night's King.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:59.800
Regardless of how you felt about it, I thought
it was amazing that they even thought to do

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:04.180
it. Based on what Dan and Dave said about
it after the fact, they just wanted to show

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:07.999
something that was going on in the book story
at that moment but wasn't something George

00:08:07.999 --> 00:08:14.399
RR Martin chose to include. Another example
would be if they showed Stannis gathering

00:08:14.399 --> 00:08:18.569
supplies and setting sail with his Army to
the Wall.

00:08:18.569 --> 00:08:22.669
Stannis was doing that, but you just don't
read about it in excruciating detail. Tycho

00:08:22.669 --> 00:08:27.529
Nestoris is kind of like, here's a giant bag
of money. Grab everyone and get your ass to

00:08:27.529 --> 00:08:29.779
the wall. You'd better pay this back.

00:08:29.779 --> 00:08:34.390
Because they said they'd be doing even more
things like this in Season 5 I feel like I

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:40.830
need to dedicate a bonus video to all the
things they could include that weren't happening

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.289
in book 4 or 5.

00:08:42.289 --> 00:08:45.870
With regards to the White Walkers, I feel
like they're just massing their forces and

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:50.210
slowly moving towards the Wall. So hopefully
in Season 5 we'll see another epic shot of

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:53.270
their army.

00:08:53.270 --> 00:09:00.270
Number 3 - The Battle of Craster's Keep

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:04.640
Another big change from the books, but something
that was necessary to tie up old plot lines.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:08.610
I loved the death they gave Burn Gorman. I
was such a fan of his on Torchwood that seeing

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:11.240
him play a crazy villain was so much fun.

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:15.120
There were a few big questions about how it
all played out and why Bran lets things go

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:19.280
so far without warging Hodor and making him
Hulk out on everyone. I wasn't a huge fan

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:23.480
of the Locke character either, but they had
to resolve his story somehow and Craster's

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:25.560
seemed like as good a time as any.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:28.640
Too bad they couldn't have postponed his death
till the Wildling Attack. It would have been

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:32.880
fun to see him get killed by the huge Arrow
the Giant fired or accidentally kill him with

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.150
that big Scythe.

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:37.570
Or maybe they could have sent him into the
tunnel with Grenn the Giantslayer, may he

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:40.100
rest in peace.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.930
Number 2 - Oberyn Martell vs The Mountain

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:47.320
This was one of the big book scenes that they
remained faithful too. They did alter the

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:53.450
death a little, and Oberyn in the book was
a little happier when he was dying, but the

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:57.410
important parts were taken right off the page
like his speech trying to goad the confession

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:58.220
out of the Mountain and the poisoned spear.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:01.610
I saw a behind the scenes video with Pedro
Pascal learning a lot of the fight choreography,

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:04.400
so it seems like he did a lot of that fight
himself. I studied Taekwondo when I was little,

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:05.610
but I never got far enough along to learn
how to use weapons.

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:10.500
Fight scenes are hard to do period, but fighting
with weapons like that is almost impossible

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.650
for someone if they're not an expert. It was
definitely the best fight scene of the season

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:16.960
and the way the filmed it was the best too.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:21.730
I loved the Brienne vs the Hound Fight scene
too, but the cinematography on it was a little

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:24.580
too much shaky cam.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:28.320
and my Number 1 Moment from Season 4 is actually
a tie so I'll just do them both - It's Arya

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:31.380
Heading to Braavos and Tyrion killing Shae
and Tywin.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:35.470
Arya heading to Braavos is such a huge turning
point for her character and it's the start

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:40.070
of her story in Book 4, a whole new book's
worth of content for her. I think that's part

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:45.070
of the reason they chose that to be the final
scene. I maintain the fire and ice ending

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:49.170
moment for each season just on the basis she's
a Stark of Winterfell. But it was a huge point

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:53.070
of departure for her story and it's a huge
transition for the show.

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:56.980
Stannis is at the Wall and taking the White
Walkers seriously, Tyrion gives the middle

00:10:56.980 --> 00:11:02.190
finger to everyone in King's Landing and takes
off. It's like transitioning from High School

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:05.570
to College or University if you're international.

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:08.610
Tyrion's moment felt like it should have been
more cathartic, but I don't think he's going

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:15.610
to feel less burdened with Tywin and Shae
dead. The relief of revenge kills is always

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.780
short lived. It's never a 100 percent solution
to all of your problems.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:19.180
I was never a huge fan of Shae's character,
I didn't even pay that much attention to her

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:21.770
in the books so when the show started using
her a lot more I was a little confused. I

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:26.090
kind of mentally wiped my hands of her when
Tyrion choked her with Tywin's chain of office.

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:29.830
Tywin's final moments were interesting for
a number of reasons. There's a big debate

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:33.680
about whether or not he was being truthful
when he said he never intended to let Tyrion

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:37.390
die. I chose to believe him the first time
I watched the episode, he definitely holds

00:11:37.390 --> 00:11:43.010
back a lot of information, but I don't remember
him outright lying.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:47.870
He did admit that he quietly took every opportunity
to let Tyrion die over the years though, so

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:52.180
he contradicts himself. I think it just means
that you can take him either way. You would

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:57.140
be equally right in saying Tywin was going
to execute Tyrion or Save him.

00:11:57.140 --> 00:12:00.700
It's like Schrodinger's Toilet.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:04.990
Since there are like a billion other huge
moments let me know what your favorites were.

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:09.370
And if you want to talk about spoilery things
that you want to books to include next season,

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.890
please just use spoiler tags in the comments.

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:18.890
So here's my answer to everyone asking for
full on Spoiler Videos. I want to make content

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:23.140
that you guys ask for, so if the majority
of you ask for something specific I try to

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:27.360
do everything I can to make it happen. The
reason I don't do spoiler videos all the time

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:31.520
is because making two videos for one thing
is just way too much. I already feel like

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:38.520
I'm not able to do all the videos I want to
do for other things like Walking Dead and

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:40.400
Doctor Who.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:46.170
Because we're into Season 5 stuff now what
I'm going to try is just designating a portion

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:52.840
of my videos for spoilery stuff. In addition,
I will be doing Book videos, videos for specific

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:59.160
book content. Like when we're talking about
prophecies and theories like Patchface, Varys

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:04.730
and Blackfyre and the Three Heads of The Dragon.

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:09.810
Because you guys have been so great this season,
my next video is going to be about Aegon The

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.180
Conqueror. That will post this Sunday. Be
sure to subscribe to get it.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:12.340
Whenever I do stuff like that it will be about
the books, not the show. Whenever I post one

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:12.590
I'll be really clear that this is a book video
not a show video. So hopefully all the book

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:12.800
readers and the show watchers will be able
to enjoy things without stepping on toes.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:17.370
I'm really proud of the way you guys all embraced
the use of spoiler tags in comments, because

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:21.620
you guys have largely been pretty good about
the way you comment it hasn't been a problem

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:27.850
here. Thank you so much for listening to that.

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:32.580
I'll say you can make any comment you want
about anything on any of my videos as long

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:38.020
as you're not committing a hate crime or trolling.
The only reason I make videos is to communicate

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:43.840
with people, so the more you comment on videos,
the happier I am.

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:48.020
I'm going to be doing a special Personal Q&amp;A
